# scc defaults. One command-line flag per line; `#` comments and blanks are
# ignored. Found via SCC_CONFIG_PATH, set in .zshenv.
#
# Precedence: this file < ./.sccconfig in a project < flags you type.

# COCOMO estimates a 1981 waterfall project's cost from line count alone, at an
# assumed $56,286 salary. It is calibrated on FORTRAN and COBOL, counts config
# and comments as engineering, and tells you nothing actionable. Off.
--no-cocomo

# Worth typing ad hoc rather than setting here:
#   --by-file        per-file breakdown instead of the per-language summary
#   --no-gen         skip generated files (lazy-lock.json and friends)
#   -a               DRYness: how much of the code is duplicated
#   --cognitive      nesting-weighted complexity, harsher than the default
#   -f json -o x     machine-readable output
